# Copy this to `.env` and fill in what you need.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` itself is gitignored and must stay that way — it is the only place a secret
# lives in this repository.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT WORKS WITHOUT ANY OF THIS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# You do NOT need a Razorpay account to evaluate this project. Measured, with every
# Razorpay variable left empty:
#
#     conformance suite, per merchant:   55 passed, 3 skipped   (of 58)
#
# The three that skip say why, by name: one is structural (all three merchants offer
# all three payment modes, so "an undeclared mode" has no case left) and two are the
# payment-instrument tests, which report `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET set
# nahi hain` rather than passing quietly.
#
# Everything else runs: all three shops, the catalog, live product detail, search
# across merchants, carts, the quantity and amount ceilings, the prompt-injection
# sanitizer, the audit log, and order creation in `cod` mode. What needs keys is the
# part where money actually moves.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MERCHANT KEYS — required, and they are not secrets in any real sense
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each merchant authenticates exactly one caller: the Layer (SPEC §2.5). These are
# shared secrets between your Layer and your own merchants, so for a local checkout
# any string works. They must simply match what the merchant is started with.
NORTHWIND_AGENT_KEY=nw_agentkey_local_dev_only
VOLTLINE_AGENT_KEY=vl_agentkey_local_dev_only
MARIGOLD_AGENT_KEY=mg_agentkey_local_dev_only

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RAZORPAY — optional; needed only for the parts where money moves
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEST MODE ONLY. Dashboard → turn Test Mode on → Settings → API Keys → Generate.
# The key id starts with `rzp_test_`. The secret never appears in any API response —
# merchants return only the publishable key id, and only for `checkout` orders.
#
# Note from experience, in case you try to pay a link by hand: the international test
# card 4111 1111 1111 1111 does NOT work on a fresh test account (international
# payments are off by default). Netbanking works, and so does UPI `success@razorpay`.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENROUTER — optional; only for `demo/buyer.py`
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drives a real LLM through the MCP tool surface, so the prompt-injection defence is
# measured against an actual model rather than asserted. Nothing else needs it. A
# whole purchase costs about $0.002 on gpt-4o-mini.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOSTING — optional
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every merchant binds 127.0.0.1 on its own fixed port by default, which is what the
# scripts and the documentation assume. A host that hands you a port sets these.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8001
